{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap, handling and return","requirement":"A lessor may not require a security deposit above one month's rent, must hold it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay 5% interest per year, and return it with an itemized list of damages within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Applies to leases of residential real property in Massachusetts; the section states no building age, unit count or ownership conditions.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"A non-refundable fee in lieu of a security deposit is allowed only under regulations, must be optional for tenant and lessor, and in total may not exceed one month's rent.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Successor-in-interest liability does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter 60, or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution.","penalty":"Where the lessor fails to deposit the funds, to transfer the deposit, or to return it within 30 days, the tenant is awarded three times the deposit or balance plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees; the lessor forfeits the right to retain any part of the deposit.","effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2);","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts limit on advance payments before tenancy","requirement":"At or before a tenancy starts, a lessor or the lessor's agent may not require a tenant to pay more than first and last month's rent, one month's rent as a security deposit, and the cost of a key and lock.","key_value":"First and last month's rent + 1 month's rent deposit + key and lock cost","coverage_conditions":"Applies to any tenancy or prospective tenancy of residential real property in Massachusetts; binds the lessor and the lessor's agent.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"The duty applies at or prior to the commencement of a tenancy.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following:  (i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and, (ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and, (iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts fee-in-lieu-of-deposit offer and credit-score limits","requirement":"Regulations for a fee in lieu of a security deposit must require the lessor to offer it to every approved applicant, regardless of income, credit score, race, gender, disability, immigration status or household size, and not to use those factors to set the fee.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Concerns regulations the executive office of housing and livable communities may adopt allowing a lessor and tenant to agree to a fee in lieu of a security deposit.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies to a lessor who offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit under those regulations, toward prospective tenants whose application for occupancy has been approved.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(E) require a lessor who offers such a fee in lieu of security deposit:  (I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;  and (II) not to consider such factors and categories when setting the amount of the fee","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.65,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
